 Document Copilot quota release and optional fallback behavior","tree":"9b4a4afd363dcf0f8d8a64f46a2a4552a1fdbaa9"}],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"08b1d51afa000ee38f294f8f9ac99b05d938323fda0bc8d96b4599687e5bf9e6","finding_commits":{"inline:4226680419":"38b1c64b9f490651856a45e742adcdc52c7bff35","inline:4226680469":"06b6dae928dc61c493f260723cdf35d030f364f7","review:5465783898":"38b1c64b9f490651856a45e742adcdc52c7bff35"},"parent":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","patch_sha256":"d3c822d46b958301b1b156ae9cc31b3fe134517040840271caf3054d5a90f84d","tree":"9b4a4afd363dcf0f8d8a64f46a2a4552a1fdbaa9"},"dispositions":{"batches":[{"analysis":"A retry restores delivered request receipts before iteration, but its fallback merge was only in memory. Save merged fallback state on token-enabled retry passes before any continue or empty-queue exit. Add regressions covering restored receipts, retained exhaustion, and later pushes.","downsides":"Adds one local fallback-state write on token-enabled retry passes, including passes with no queued requests.","findings":["review:5465783898","inline:4226680419"],"length":4642,"offset":0,"sha256":"c2c9fb45c683516491dd127539efb337b848513c2cd396632b814096e1680d4d","summary":"Persist merged Copilot fallback state before CAS retry skips","upsides":"Preserves the original quota baseline and exhausted status across rejected CAS pushes, preventing another request from an exhausted fallback requester."},{"analysis":"The README described a current-head review as unconditional, although quota exhaustion disables only the Copilot gate without an available fallback. Document the optional requester, new-notice exhaustion, persistence across pushes, and unaffected required-check and feedback blockers; align the corresponding rationale.","downsides":"Adds operator-facing detail that must stay aligned with future quota and fallback policy changes.","findings":["inline:4226680469"],"length":8531,"offset":4642,"sha256":"e493d2f680d293b29a248139b7cab299454bb67ab89ed91af478592311127807","summary":"Document Copilot quota release and optional fallback behavior","upsides":"Operators can predict routing without a completed Copilot review and understand when configuring a fallback keeps the normal gate active."}],"findings":[{"analysis":"Investigated the complete overview and both linked details. Its primary CAS-loss claim is confirmed: restored receipts skip delivery while the fallback merge remains unsaved. The persistence batch fixes that root cause; the separate documentation batch addresses the overview's other linked finding.","disposition":"fixed","downsides":"Retry passes perform an additional local state write; documentation now includes the fallback exception.","key":"review:5465783898","upsides":"Prevents a lost quota baseline from allowing another exhausted-fallback request and explains the remaining routing gates."},{"analysis":"Confirmed at the frozen head and reproduced with two failing regressions. Persist the merged fallback records before iteration so a restored delivered receipt or empty queue cannot lose quota IDs or exhaustion. The tests also verify that a later push cannot trigger another request after fallback exhaustion.","disposition":"fixed","downsides":"Adds a fallback-state write on each token-enabled retry pass, even when every request is skipped.","key":"inline:4226680419","upsides":"Retains durable fallback identity and exhaustion through CAS reset/retry without changing normal request delivery or no-token behavior."},{"analysis":"Confirmed against copilot_reviews_disabled, evaluation facts, routing, and workflow secret wiring. The README and rationale now state that quota exhaustion releases only the Copilot gate without a configured fallback or after the fallback is exhausted, and explain the optional fallback and later-push behavior.","disposition":"fixed","downsides":"The expanded policy description must be maintained if fallback behavior changes.","key":"inline:4226680469","upsides":"Makes reviewless routing predictable while explicitly retaining required-check and actionable-feedback blockers."}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"8c977f83e759b60d827b7a3c41f047c839ca8d495226659fa056a5c429c089b4","schema":2},"download_sha256":"3ad85e46d2b5123ad3d691458b449d15284fee89db3978c80aa6077a5812a3f2","frozen_sha":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","pr":452,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/shared-workflows","request_digest":"8c977f83e759b60d827b7a3c41f047c839ca8d495226659fa056a5c429c089b4","request_id":"f4a17224e1a54f9188f2195ed498f702","run_attempt":1,"run_id":37886022192,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:3ad85e46d2b5123ad3d691458b449d15284fee89db3978c80aa6077a5812a3f2","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":37886896244},"workflow_revision":"eadecd0ffce9590595791925dd85130dae808235"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5464843292,5465783898],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nCAS retries can lose fallback state and permit another request from an exhausted fallback requester.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open findings</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Persist merged fallback state across CAS retry failures](#discussion_r4226680419) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Document Copilot gate release behavior without fallback](#discussion_r4226680469) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5465783898","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5465783898},{"body":"The retry snapshot is merged only into the in-memory `fallbacks` mapping. After a CAS push failure, the next attempt can skip every request because the request receipt was also restored, so this mapping is never saved and the fallback record created by the failed attempt is lost. A later push can then treat all existing quota notices as the baseline and send another request from the already exhausted fallback requester. Persist the merged fallback state before any loop `continue` paths, and add a CAS-retry regression test.","comment_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","comment_id":4226680419,"key":"inline:4226680419","kind":"inline","line":78,"original_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","original_line":78,"path":".github/scripts/pull-request-dashboard/copilot_review_delivery.py","review_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","review_id":5465783898,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"e8f324dffd677977805254b91edd867f17adebaf3354c66378a49a2e45fb700f","id":4226680419,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDOTENyc86qpcTr"},{"body":"The documented gate semantics no longer match the implementation. This still says a clean Copilot review is required and that a quota notice does not count as a review, but the new logic immediately releases the Copilot gate when no fallback token is configured (or after the fallback is exhausted), while retaining required-check and actionable-feedback blockers. Please document that release behavior, including the optional fallback case, so operators can predict when a PR routes without a completed review.","comment_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","comment_id":4226680469,"key":"inline:4226680469","kind":"inline","line":142,"original_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","original_line":142,"path":"pull-request-dashboard/README.md","review_commit_id":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","review_id":5465783898,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"836c043d151afd0f0dd227ef121c4c51402b9fdb1374edaede0c2ff2ae5e080e","id":4226680469,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T04:44:06Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDOTENyc86qpcUN"}],"frozen_at":1791521602,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-09T04:53:22Z","frozen_sha":"21a180b6fc557f65436fc14bb6dafa1bdc57df8f","head_ref":"trask-copilot-review-loop","head_repo":"open-telemetry/shared-workflows","head_repo_id":1279488627,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":37884850288},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","mode":"publish","pr":452,"protocol":"reviewable-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791520741,"generation":2,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"75b132153145437f916a64645a612689","profile":"reviewable-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/shared-workflows","repo_id":1279488627,"request_id":"f4a17224e1a54f9188f2195ed498f702","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/eadecd0ffce9590595791925dd85130dae808235","workflow_revision":"eadecd0ffce9590595791925dd85130dae808235"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":37886022192,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/37886022192"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":["c2f8fd163056601cdd4b0384d140e0a3fffde63585cd04952d18db559c7ff773"],"seen_inline_findings":["89b6523960ef066454cfe0006753d1d5d273c7c39f4935752e9e8d82eb2c83d6","e5c5f0977d9fe4058b67c9a638b818851fb8079e6fc70e6471563363665a564d"],"seen_missed_findings":[],"stage":"thread_effects","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":37886896244}}